      <p>The constructions that make the Quran precise: conditionals, exception, emphasis, the mafʿul family, and the weak verbs that bend the rules. It ends with a full analysis of Ad-Duha.</p>
      <div class="chips"><span>Conditionals</span><span>The mafʿul family</span><span>Weak verbs</span><span>Rhetoric</span><span>Checkpoint: Ad-Duha</span></div>
      <div class="ct" data-ct>Not started</div>
    </div>

    <div class="card" data-stop="5">
      <span class="rn">Level 5 · {totals[5]} lessons</span>
      <h2>Applied Study <span lang="ar" dir="rtl">التطبيق القرآني</span></h2>
      <p>Everything turned on the Book itself: complete analyses of Al-Fatiha and Ayat al-Kursi, Quranic patterns, narrative and rhetoric — until you can parse a passage you have never studied.</p>
      <div class="chips"><span>The method</span><span>Applied analyses</span><span>Narrative &amp; dialogue</span><span>Capstone: cold read</span></div>
      <div class="ct" data-ct>Not started — the capstone waits</div>
